---Archive Tunnel
---
---The Tunnels API is in research preview. It requires the `anthropic-beta: mcp-tunnels-2026-06-22` header and may change without a deprecation period. It supersedes the Admin API endpoints at `/v1/organizations/tunnels`, which remain available during a migration window.
---
---Archives a tunnel. Archival is irreversible: every non-archived certificate on the tunnel is archived in the same operation, the hostname is retired and never re-allocated, and the tunnel token is invalidated. Retrying against an already-archived tunnel returns the existing record unchanged.
---
---`POST /v1/tunnels/{tunnel_id}/archive`
---@param input anthropic.beta_tunnels.ArchiveTunnelRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_tunnels.BetaTunnel? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:archive_tunnel(input) end

---Archive Tunnel Certificate
---
---The Tunnels API is in research preview. It requires the `anthropic-beta: mcp-tunnels-2026-06-22` header and may change without a deprecation period. It supersedes the Admin API endpoints at `/v1/organizations/tunnels`, which remain available during a migration window.
---
---Archives a tunnel certificate, removing it from the set Anthropic trusts for the tunnel. The certificate record is retained. Archiving the last non-archived certificate is permitted; the tunnel rejects MCP traffic until a new certificate is added.
---
---`POST /v1/tunnels/{tunnel_id}/certificates/{certificate_id}/archive`
---@param input anthropic.beta_tunnels.ArchiveTunnelCertificateRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_tunnels.BetaTunnelCertificate? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:archive_tunnel_certificate(input) end

---Create Tunnel
---
---The Tunnels API is in research preview. It requires the `anthropic-beta: mcp-tunnels-2026-06-22` header and may change without a deprecation period. It supersedes the Admin API endpoints at `/v1/organizations/tunnels`, which remain available during a migration window.
---
---Creates a tunnel. Creation allocates a fresh hostname and provisions the tunnel; it is not idempotent. The new tunnel rejects MCP traffic until at least one CA certificate is added.
---
---`POST /v1/tunnels`
---@param input? anthropic.beta_tunnels.CreateTunnelRequest
---@return anthropic.beta_tunnels.BetaTunnel? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
